card.statement:
The graph

\[
\xymatrix@R=14pt@C=14pt{
1\ar@{.}[d]&1'&1''\ar@{.}[ld]\\
2&2'
\\}
\]

gives the problem of classifying partitioned arrays $\u A=[\u A_{\alpha \beta 1}]$ consisting of $2\cdot 2\cdot 1$ spatial blocks up to $(R\oplus R^{-T},S\oplus U^{-T},U)$-transformations; that is, up to linked block-equivalence transformations

\[
\xymatrix@R=7pt@C=14pt{
&*{}\ar@{-}[rrrr]&&*{}&&*{}\\
*{}\ar@{-}[ur]|{\,U\,}
\ar@{-}[rr]|{\,S\,}
&&*{}
\ar@{-}[rr]|{\;U^{-T}}&&*{}\\
&&&&&*{}\\
*{}\ar@{}[rruu]|{\pmb{\u A_{111}}}\ar@{-}[uu]|{R\vphantom{A^A_A}}
\ar@{-}'[rrrr][rrrrru]&&*{}
\ar@{}[rruu]|{\pmb{\u A_{121}}}
&&*{}\\
&&&&&*{}\\
*{}\ar@{}[rruu]|{\pmb{\u A_{211}}}
\ar@{-}[uu]|{R^{-T}}\ar@{-}'[rrrr]'[rrrruuuu]
&&*{}\ar@{}[rruu]|{\pmb{\u A_{221}}}
\ar@{-}'[uuuu][uuuuur]&&*{}\ar@{-}'[ru]'[ruuuuu][uuuu]\\
}
\]

This problem can be considered as the problem of classifying array-representations
$\mathcal A=(\u A_{111},\u A_{121},\u A_{211},\u A_{221})$ of the directed bipartite
graph

\[
\xymatrix@R=-6pt@C=10ex{
t_{111}
\ar@/^/@{<-}[rd]
\ar@/^/@{<-}[rddd]
\ar@/^/@{<-}[rddddd]\\
&{r\quad}
\\
t_{121}
\ar@/_3pt/@{<-}[ru]
\ar@<-0.5ex>@/^9pt/@{->}[rddd]
\ar@<-0.5ex>@/^5pt/@{<-}[rddd]\\
&{s\quad }
\\
t_{211}
\ar@/_3pt/@{->}[ruuu]
\ar@<-0.3ex>@{<-}[ru]
\ar@<-0.5ex>@/^3pt/@{<-}[rd]
\\
&{u\quad }
\\
t_{221}
\ar@/_9pt/@{->}[ruuuuu]
\ar@/_1pt/@{->}[ru]
\ar@<-0.1ex>@/_/@{<-}[ru]
\\
}
\]
